    "body": "Adds one line to `_ROCM_DEVICE_ID_NAME_MAP` in `vllm/platforms/rocm.py`:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n     \"0x744c\": \"AMD_Radeon_RX7900XTX\",\r\n+    \"0x744b\": \"AMD_Radeon_PRO_W7900D\",  # Navi 31, gfx1100\r\n```\r\n\r\nWithout it, `get_device_name()` falls back to `asic_info[\"market_name\"]`, which on this card is\r\nthe generic string `\"AMD Radeon Graphics\"`. `get_device_name_as_file_name()` builds the FP8\r\nblock-quantized GEMM config filename from that, so every RDNA3 workstation card that isn't in\r\nthe map resolves to the same filename. Makes it impossible to ship a tuned config for one\r\nwithout it also applying to the others.\r\n\r\npci.ids has `0x744b` as `Navi 31 [Radeon Pro W7900D]`. I went with `AMD_Radeon_PRO_W7900D` to\r\nmatch `AMD_Radeon_RX7900XTX` / `AMD_Radeon_RX9070XT`, but `AMD_Radeon_W7900D` is fine too if\r\nyou prefer, just say and I'll change it.\r\n\r\nI checked the config directory before opening this, since renaming changes which file gets\r\nlooked up: 244 config JSONs plus a README, and zero `AMD_Radeon_*` files (the AMD entries are\r\nMI300X / MI325X / MI325_OAM, rest is Intel B70 and NVIDIA). Worth knowing that `0x744c`\r\n`AMD_Radeon_RX7900XTX` is already in this map and still has no config files at all, so a name\r\nentry doesn't imply a shipped config. Nothing in-tree gets invalidated. The only thing to\r\nmention in release notes is that someone who hand-dropped a config under\r\n`AMD_Radeon_Graphics` would need to rename it.\r\n\r\nTested by applying the diff and re-importing in a fresh process:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> from vllm.platforms import current_platform\r\n>>> from vllm.utils.platform_utils import get_device_name_as_file_name\r\n>>> current_platform.get_device_name(0)\r\n'AMD_Radeon_PRO_W7900D'      # was 'AMD Radeon Graphics'\r\n>>> get_device_name_as_file_name()\r\n'AMD_Radeon_PRO_W7900D'      # was 'AMD_Radeon_Graphics'\r\n```\r\n\r\nI didn't run `pytest tests/platforms/` — no pytest in my ROCm venv. It's